On Mon, Apr 6, 2015 at 3:39 AM, Gleki Arxokuna <gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com>
wrote:

>
> E.g. I proposed adding " / COhE_elidible" where COhE_elidible returns a "
> { ... } " expression.
>

Currently your rule is called GOhA_elidible, but I think that's the wrong
name for what it does, it should be "selbri_elided", since it replaces
"selbri", not "GOhA", and the rule succeeds only when the selbri is in fact
elidED. The _elidIBLE rules succeed both when the construct is elided and
when not elided.

A GOhA_elidible rule would have to replace GOhA_clause (although that would
allow many more perhaps not desirable things to be grammatical).

